Write two sentences explaining why this colour might suit your users and application.

Red on black gives FuelFare a sleek, dashboard-style look that fits an app about cars and driving. Red also draws attention, so it works well for the most important things, like the total trip cost and the Calculate button.

One design tip for later: this red has enough contrast for text on a white background, but on pure black it’s a bit too dark for small text. In dark mode, use it for buttons and accents, and use a lighter red (like #FF4D5E) if you need red text. Your colour ramp from the tool will give you those lighter shades.

